      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The University of Michigan moved to Ann Arbor in 1837 from Detroit, where it was founded in 1817, and has driven the city’s growth ever since.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.britannica.com/place/Ann-Arbor",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1839, the Michigan Central Railroad turned Ann Arbor into a regional transportation hub, linking it to Detroit and the Midwest.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ann_Arbor%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Ann Arbor Hands‑On Museum, housed in a renovated historic downtown fire station, offers interactive science exhibits for all ages.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
